  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed two storey, side extension would infill the gap between the neighbouring semi-detached house, in a street where narrow separation distances between houses are a marked feature of the character and appearance of the street. As such, the character and appearance of the street would be eroded to its detriment. The proposed rear brown cladding would harm the character and appearance of the host dwelling as well as the wider surrounding area, by reason of its extent of coverage across the dwelling. The proposal would, therefore, fail to comply with Policy D4 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies D12.1, D12.3 and D12.4 of the Local Plan 2024.",
    "Reason : 2 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\"\tOffering a pre-application advice and duty desk service. \r\n\"\tWhere possible, suggesting solutions to secure a successful outcome.\r\n\"\tAs appropriate, updating applicants/agents of any issues that may arise in the processing of their application.\r\nIn this instance\r\n\"\tIt is noted that the applicant/agent did not engage in any pre-application discussions.\r\n\"\tThe applicant is advised to seek pre-application advice on any resubmission.\r\n"
  ],
